      "requirement_name": "Emergency removal hearing",
      "deadline": "Hearing on the next court day (the Division must cause a complaint to be filed within two court days after the removal, N.J.S.A. 9:6-8.30(b))",
      "starts_from": "Child's emergency (“Dodd”) removal from the home without a court order",
      "source": "state_statute",
      "source_url": "https://law.justia.com/codes/new-jersey/title-9/section-9-6-8-31/",
      "consequence_of_miss": "If there has been no hearing on the removal at which the parent or guardian was present or had an adequate opportunity to be present, the parent or guardian may apply for a hearing on returning the child, which must be held within three court days of the application except for good cause shown (N.J.S.A. 9:6-8.32)."
    },
